  "worked_solution": "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{PU}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{RS}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{ST}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/2492594432bf29b2753d646c53b66ffd6230c21db71c4dd12479c9811217dc91.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{UP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{RS}$ and $\\overset{―}{ST}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{UP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}$ and $\\overset{―}{RS}⊥\\overset{―}{ST}$",
